### Page 1 of 2

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: "A RESOLUTION EXPRESSING THE DETERMINATION BY THE
GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE FOR THE REPEAL
OF ENACTING RESOLUTIONS AND DISSOLUTION OF SPECIFIC CITY
COMMITTEES,
COMMISSIONS
AND
COUNCILS
DUE
TO
INACTIVITY."

WHEREAS, recently the overall administration of the City’s committees, commissions and
councils has been a topic of concern with residents and councilmembers;

WHEREAS, the City’s website in certain respects provides inaccurate information
regarding the activity of City appointed committees, commissions and councils, which impairs
transparency of the work these administrative bodies conduct on behalf of the City;

WHEREAS, the website for the City of Cheyenne includes information for City
committees, commissions and councils that are no longer active or whose mission has been re-
assigned, fulfilled or has become obsolete;

WHEREAS, pursuant to Resolution #4841, adopted by the Governing Body on June 26,
2006, the City of Cheyenne created the Greater Cheyenne Arts Advisory Council. It is unknown
when this advisory council ceased conducting business on behalf of the City;

WHEREAS; despite its cease of operations, the mission of the Greater Cheyenne Arts
Advisory Council has been continued through the creation of “Arts in Public Places,” an advisory
committee that seeks to encourage and enhance artistic expression and appreciation, and add value
to the community through acquisition, exhibition and maintenance of public art;

WHEREAS, pursuant to Resolution #4932, adopted by the Governing Body on April 9,
2007, the City of Cheyenne created the Cheyenne Community Forestry Committee. It is
understood that this committee has not met in over a decade;

WHEREAS; while the forestry committee has long since gone inactive, its mission has
been embraced by Rooted in Cheyenne, a nonprofit organization that works in partnership with
the Cheyenne Urban Forestry Division and is dedicated to improving Cheyenne’s urban forest;

WHEREAS, pursuant to Ordinance #2948, adopted by the Governing Body on May 27,
1986, the City of Cheyenne created the City of Cheyenne Personnel Commission. The purpose of
this commission was to provide aid in the interpretation of City employee rules and regulations, to
consider and decide employee grievances, and to make recommendations to the Mayor and City
Council; and

10:03 am, Oct 09, 2024
```

### Page 2 of 2

```text
WHEREAS, the personnel commission over the years became increasingly less active,
culminating in the termination of the commission by the Governing Body through the adoption of
Ordinance #4368 on June 14, 2021. Despite its termination, information specific to this
commission can still be found on the website for the City of Cheyenne.

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE CITY
OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that the Governing Body recognizes that due to inactivity,
redistribution of duties, and dissolvement of the above-referenced committees, commissions and
councils, that each should now be considered terminated and their authority otherwise repealed,
and that they no longer be regulated by the City of Cheyenne.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of _____________________,
2024.

__________________________________________
Patrick Collins, Mayor

(SEAL)

ATTEST:

____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
```
